A young waiter approaches me.
He has a tray in his hand.
The chai and bun maska are on the tray.
There is not much space here.
So I place my bag elsewhere.
I make some space on the table.
I look at the waiter.
I say, "Please place the chai here."
The waiter smiles.
He places the chai on the table.
He places the bun maska there too.
He says, "Madam, here is the chai."
I smile.
I say, "Thank you very much."
He asks, "Is anything else needed?"
I tell him, "No, it is enough for now."
The waiter walks away from there.
The aroma of the bun maska is very good.
The chai is also very hot.
Now I am very happy.
